---
import Base from "../layouts/Base.astro";
import Bow from "../components/Bow.astro";
import Waterline from "../components/Waterline.astro";
import IconLighter from "../components/IconLighter.astro";
import IconDrydock from "../components/IconDrydock.astro";
import RidingHigher from "../components/RidingHigher.astro";
import { stock, tier8, mb, SOUNDING_HREF } from "../lib/trim-sounding";
import { logbookEntries, formatDate } from "../lib/logbook";

const recent = (await logbookEntries()).slice(0, 3);
---
<Base>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="wrap hero-grid">
      <div class="headline">
        <h1 class="hull">The tools we use to make our stories.</h1>
      </div>
      <div class="above">
        <p class="sub">
          Salvage is Chapterists' open-source toolbox. Chapterists is a story company, and making stories takes a lot
          of tools. When one we've built is worth keeping, we haul it up, clean it off and share it here, under the MIT
          license.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="bow-cell">
        <Bow />
      </div>
      <div class="below">
        <p class="tagline hull">First in the hold: Unreal Engine, lighter on low-RAM machines and better on a Mac.</p>
        <p class="caption">Draft marks in gigabytes: a game that carries less memory rides higher. (An illustration, not a measurement.)</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--deep-sea)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" stripe="var(--antifouling)" />

  <section class="why wrap">
    <h2 class="hull">Every project leaves good tools behind.</h2>
    <div class="why-copy">
      <p>
        A script that fixed a build. A check that caught a problem before it cost a day. A setting that made a slow
        machine usable. Most of what a team builds to get the work done stays buried in the project that needed it.
      </p>
      <p>
        Salvage is where we bring those up. A tool comes aboard when it's useful beyond the job it was made for, and
        it goes on the <a href="/manifest/">manifest</a> with what it does and what it changes.
      </p>
      <p>It starts with Unreal Engine. More tools will join as our stories need them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground)" below="var(--ground-2)" shape="angle" />

  <section class="unreal">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="hull">Your machine has more in it than you think.</h2>
      <div class="unreal-copy">
        <p class="lede">The first two workstreams are about Unreal Engine.</p>
        <p>
          RAM is expensive right now, and high-end games keep asking for more of it. A machine gets written off when
          a game or an editor wants more memory than it has, and upgrading is the usual answer. We would rather find
          out how much of that memory the work really needs, and cut what it doesn't.
        </p>
        <p>
          A fix like that helps everyone. The old laptop gets a game that runs. The big workstation gets its memory
          back.
        </p>
        <p class="tagline hull">We don't sell you a new ship. We get yours sailing.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground-2)" below="var(--rescue-orange)" shape="angle-reverse" />
  <section class="punchout">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="hull">Somebody called your machine a wreck. <span>We'd like a look at it.</span></h2>
      <p>
        Laptops with 8 GB of memory. Desktops a few graphics cards behind. The Mac you were told isn't for game
        development. Those are the machines we're working for.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
  <Waterline above="var(--rescue-orange)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" />

  <section class="streams wrap" aria-labelledby="streams-title">
    <h2 class="hull streams-title" id="streams-title">The first two workstreams</h2>

    <article class="stream" id="lighter-unreal">
      <IconLighter class="stream-icon" />
      <div>
        <h3 class="hull">Lighter Unreal</h3>
        <p class="lede">Make Unreal Engine games and the editor run on lower-powered machines, memory first.</p>
        <p>
          A lighter is a barge that takes cargo off a ship so it can float into shallow water. Same job here: take
          load off the engine so big games fit on small
          machines. <a href="/charts/unreal-memory-on-16-gb/">Where Unreal's memory goes on a 16 GB machine</a> explains what
          we're up against.
        </p>
        <p class="now">
          In the box: <a href="/charts/salvage-trim/"><code>salvage trim</code></a> gives a project memory tiers for 8,
          12 and 16 GB machines, and <a href="/charts/salvage-soundings/"><code>salvage soundings</code></a> reads a
          memory capture and shows where the memory goes, and whether the run fits.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>

    <article class="stream">
      <IconDrydock class="stream-icon" />
      <div>
        <h3 class="hull">Unreal on Mac</h3>
        <p class="lede">Make developing with Unreal Engine on macOS fast and pleasant.</p>
        <p>
          Plenty of people build games on a Mac. The editor, the builds and the tools around them should feel like
          they belong there, not like they're putting up with it.
        </p>
        <p class="now">
          In the box: <a href="/charts/salvage-doctor/"><code>salvage doctor</code></a> runs 12 checks on a Mac for
          the things that make Unreal slow or broken, <a href="/charts/salvage-lldb/"><code>salvage lldb</code></a> makes
          Unreal types readable in Xcode and LLDB, <a href="/charts/salvage-clangd/"><code>salvage clangd</code></a> sets
          up VS Code or Neovim for Unreal C++, and <a href="/charts/salvage-refit/"><code>salvage refit</code></a> rebuilds
          Windows-only plugins for Mac where the source allows it. It got Epic's PSD
          importer <a href="/soundings/refit-ue58-mac/">importing a PSD in the Mac editor</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </article>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground)" below="var(--night-sea)" shape="angle" />

  <section class="measured" aria-labelledby="measured-title">
    <div class="wrap measured-grid">
      <div class="measured-copy">
        <h2 class="hull" id="measured-title">Measured, not guessed.</h2>
        <p>
          The first sounding is in. On Epic's Third Person template on a 16 GB Mac, <code>salvage trim</code>'s 8 GB
          tier took the game from {mb(stock.mem)} MB to {mb(tier8.mem)} MB, and the frame rate didn't move.
        </p>
        <p>
          It's one small project on one machine, and the smaller tiers ran on a 16 GB Mac rather than on 8 and 12 GB
          ones. <a href={SOUNDING_HREF}>The sounding</a> has the method, the spread across runs, the frame-time cost
          and the list of what it doesn't show yet.
        </p>
      </div>
      <RidingHigher compact />
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--night-sea)" below="var(--ground-2)" shape="angle-reverse" />

  <section class="built">
    <div class="wrap">
      <h2 class="hull built-title">How it's built</h2>
      <dl>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">Tools ship here.</dt>
          <dd>Standalone tools live in the Salvage repository, under the MIT license.</dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">Engine fixes go to Epic.</dt>
          <dd>
            Changes that belong inside Unreal Engine go upstream to Epic Games as pull requests, so they reach
            everyone who uses the engine, not only people who find this project.
          </dd>
        </div>
        <div>
          <dt class="hull">No engine source here.</dt>
          <dd>
            Unreal Engine source stays under Epic's license. A check on every commit keeps it out of this
            repository.
          </dd>
        </div>
      </dl>
    </div>
  </section>

  <Waterline above="var(--ground-2)" below="var(--ground)" shape="angle-reverse" />

  <section class="deck wrap">
    <div>
      <h2 class="hull">One tool in the box. No release yet.</h2>
      <p>
        The first tool is the <code>salvage</code> command, with six jobs so
        far: <code>doctor</code>, <code>soundings</code>, <code>trim</code>, <code>lldb</code>, <code>clangd</code> and <code>refit</code>. You
        can <a href="/charts/salvage-doctor/#get-salvage">build it from source</a> today. There's nothing to download
        yet.
      </p>
      <p>
        Trim is the first job that saves memory. Doctor finds what's wrong with a Mac's setup, and soundings measures
        where a game's memory goes, which is how we find what to fix and check the fixes. Every change that cuts memory
        goes on the <a href="/manifest/">manifest</a> with its <a href="/soundings/">soundings</a>: before-and-after
        numbers on named machines.
      </p>
    </div>
    <div class="log">
      <h3>From the logbook</h3>
      <ol>
        {recent.map((e) => (
          <li>
            <time datetime={formatDate(e.data.date)}>{formatDate(e.data.date)}</time>
            <span>{e.data.title}</span>
          </li>
        ))}
      </ol>
      <a href="/logbook/">Read the whole logbook</a>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>

<style>
  /* ---- Hero ---- */
  .hero {
    --bow-w: min(40vw, 36rem);
    --below-h: calc(var(--bow-w) * 0.4615);
    background: var(--night-sea);
    color: var(--foam);
    overflow: hidden;
  }
  .hero-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 1fr) var(--bow-w);
    grid-template-rows: auto 1fr var(--below-h);
    column-gap: var(--s-7);
    padding-top: var(--s-8);
  }
  .headline {
    grid-column: 1 / -1;
    grid-row: 1;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding-bottom: var(--s-5);
  }
  .above {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 2;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    padding-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .bow-cell {
    grid-column: 2;
    grid-row: 2 / 4;
    align-self: end;
  }
  .below {
    grid-column: 1;
    grid-row: 3;
    position: relative;
    z-index: 1;
    display: flex;
    flex-direction: column;
    justify-content: center;
  }
  h1 {
    font-size: clamp(2.5rem, 1rem + 4.6vw, 5.5rem);
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 24ch;
  }
  .sub {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--steel);
    max-width: 34rem;
    margin: var(--s-5) 0 0;
  }
  .tagline {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 800;
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 22ch;
  }
  .caption {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--sea-glass);
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .hero {
      --bow-w: min(78vw, 26rem);
    }
    .hero-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      grid-template-rows: auto;
      padding-top: var(--s-7);
    }
    .headline,
    .above {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
    }
    .above {
      padding: 0 0 var(--s-6);
    }
    .bow-cell {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
      width: var(--bow-w);
      justify-self: end;
      margin-right: calc(var(--gutter) * -1);
    }
    .below {
      grid-column: 1;
      grid-row: auto;
      background: var(--deep-sea);
      box-shadow: 0 0 0 100vmax var(--deep-sea);
      clip-path: inset(0 -100vmax);
      padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-4);
    }
  }

  /* ---- Shared section bits ---- */
  h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    margin: 0;
  }

  /* ---- Why ---- */
  .why h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.2rem + 2.6vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .why {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-4);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    column-gap: var(--s-8);
  }
  .why-copy {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
    color: var(--text);
  }
  .why-copy p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .why-copy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }

  /* ---- The Unreal workstreams' pitch ---- */
  .unreal {
    background: var(--ground-2);
    padding-block: var(--s-7) var(--s-6);
  }
  .unreal .wrap {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    column-gap: var(--s-8);
  }
  .unreal h2 {
    font-size: clamp(2rem, 1.2rem + 2.6vw, 3.5rem);
  }
  .unreal-copy {
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.6;
  }
  .unreal-copy p {
    margin: 0;
  }
  .unreal-copy p + p {
    margin-top: var(--s-4);
  }
  .unreal-copy .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.45;
  }
  .unreal-copy .tagline {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    margin-top: var(--s-5);
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .unreal .wrap {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--s-5);
    }
  }

  /* ---- The punchout: Rescue Orange, used big once ---- */
  .punchout {
    background: var(--rescue-orange);
    color: var(--night-sea); /* 5.75:1 */
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
  }
  .punchout h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-5);
    max-width: 21ch;
    line-height: 0.98;
  }
  .punchout h2 span {
    display: block;
  }
  .punchout p {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    font-weight: 600;
    line-height: 1.5;
    max-width: 36rem;
    margin: var(--s-6) 0 0;
  }

  /* ---- Workstreams ---- */
  .streams {
    padding-block: var(--s-7) var(--s-5);
  }
  .streams-title,
  .built-title {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-5);
  }
  .stream {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: 8rem minmax(0, 1fr);
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-block: var(--s-7);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
    max-width: 58rem;
  }
  .stream :global(.stream-icon) {
    width: 8rem;
    height: 8rem;
    filter: drop-shadow(0 10px 18px rgb(0 0 0 / 0.28));
    transition: transform 0.45s cubic-bezier(0.34, 1.56, 0.64, 1);
  }
  .stream:hover :global(.stream-icon) {
    transform: translateY(-4px) rotate(-4deg);
  }
  .stream h3 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
    margin: 0;
  }
  .stream p {
    margin: var(--s-3) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }
  .lede {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.45;
    font-weight: 600;
  }
  .now {
    font-weight: 600;
    margin-top: var(--s-4) !important;
  }
  .now a {
    color: var(--mark);
  }
  .now code,
  .deck code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.84em;
    font-weight: 500;
  }

  /* ---- The first sounding ---- */
  .measured {
    background: var(--night-sea);
    color: var(--foam);
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
  }
  .measured-grid {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 7fr);
    gap: var(--s-7);
    align-items: center;
  }
  .measured h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-4);
    max-width: 12ch;
  }
  .measured p {
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    line-height: 1.6;
    color: var(--steel);
    max-width: 30rem;
  }
  .measured p:first-of-type {
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--foam);
  }
  .measured a {
    color: var(--sea-glass);
  }
  .measured code {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.84em;
  }
  .measured :global(.riding) {
    padding: 0;
    border-bottom: 0;
  }
  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .measured-grid {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-5);
    }
  }

  /* ---- How it's built ---- */
  .built {
    background: var(--ground-2);
    padding-block: var(--s-6) var(--s-7);
  }
  dl {
    margin: 0;
    max-width: 62rem;
  }
  dl > div {
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 5fr) minmax(0, 6fr);
    gap: var(--s-6);
    padding-block: var(--s-5);
    border-top: 2px solid var(--rule);
  }
  dt {
    font-size: var(--step-2);
    font-weight: 800;
  }
  dd {
    margin: 0;
    color: var(--text);
    padding-top: 0.3rem;
  }

  /* ---- Where things stand ---- */
  .deck {
    padding-block: var(--s-8) var(--s-8);
    display: grid;
    grid-template-columns: minmax(0, 7fr) minmax(0, 5fr);
    gap: var(--s-8);
    align-items: start;
  }
  .deck h2 {
    font-size: var(--step-3);
  }
  .deck p {
    margin: var(--s-4) 0 0;
    max-width: var(--measure);
    font-size: var(--step-1);
    line-height: 1.55;
  }
  .log h3 {
    font-stretch: var(--stretch-sign);
    font-size: var(--step-0);
    font-weight: 750;
    margin: 0.4rem 0 var(--s-4);
  }
  .log ol {
    list-style: none;
    margin: 0 0 var(--s-5);
    padding: 0;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--antifouling);
  }
  .log li {
    padding: 0 0 var(--s-4) var(--s-4);
    display: grid;
    gap: 0.15rem;
  }
  .log time {
    font-family: var(--font-mono);
    font-size: 0.75rem;
    color: var(--muted);
  }
  .log span {
    font-weight: 600;
  }

  @media (max-width: 860px) {
    .why,
    .deck {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      row-gap: var(--s-5);
    }
    .stream {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-4);
    }
    .stream :global(.stream-icon) {
      width: 5.5rem;
      height: 5.5rem;
    }
    dl > div {
      grid-template-columns: 1fr;
      gap: var(--s-2);
    }
  }
</style>
